ProsperoSunshine: no Error line for the port watch's RTSP connection

The host's port watch (main_ps5.cpp, wait_or_ports_lost) connects to the RTSP port every 5 s and closes the connection
again. While a launch waits for its client, such a connection gets the waiting session and is read from, and its close
was logged as "Error: RTSP: handle_read_plaintext(): Couldn't read from tcp socket: End of file" (with encrypted RTSP as
handle_read_encrypted_header, followed by a 400 nobody reads). It is no error: a connection closed before it sent anything
is now a debug line. One that ends inside a request stays an error.

